<title>USA: U.S. mortgage application volume fell in latest wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. mortgage application volume fell in latest wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of U.S. mortgage applications fell 17.1 percent in the week ended December 20, according to a Mortgage Bankers Association of America weekly survey.</p>
<p>Specifically, the volume of applications to refinance mortgages fell 24.2 percent in the latest survey week, while applications to purchase mortgages fell 13.5 percent.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted refinancing index fell 24.2 percent to 360.4 from a revised 475.4 the previous week.</p>
<p>The purchase index fell 12.1 percent to 180.0 in the latest survey from 204.7 in the previous week.  </p>
